{"name":"Liberace","hex":"#ccb8d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Liberace","blocks":[{"text":"Władziu Valentino Liberace was an American pianist, singer, and actor. He was born in Wisconsin to parents of Italian and Polish origin and enjoyed a career spanning four decades of concerts, recordings, television, motion pictures, and endorsements. At the height of his fame, from the 1950s to 1970s, he was the highest-paid entertainer in the world, with established concert residencies in Las Vegas and an international touring schedule."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Liberace_18_Allan_Warren.jpg/330px-Liberace_18_Allan_Warren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberace","wikidata":"Q347528"},{"title":"Liberace (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Liberace is a surname. Notable people the name include:"},{"items":["Władziu Valentino Liberace (1919–1987), known mononymously as Liberace, American pianist, singer, and actor","George Liberace (1911–1983), American musician and television performer","Robert Liberace, American painter"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberace_(surname)","wikidata":"Q62226586"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/LiberaceChristmasCostume.jpg/500px-LiberaceChristmasCostume.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/LiberaceChristmasCostume.jpg/500px-LiberaceChristmasCostume.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Liberace's early-1980s Christmas costume, worn at the Las Vegas Hilton and Radio City Music Hall: Designed by Michael Travis, with fur design by Anna Nateece, the costume was one of many at the Liberace Museum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiberaceChristmasCostume.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://